      "ai": {
        "model": "deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 11,
        "title": "Luna per-model daily cap raised from 2 to 3 sessions",
        "summary": "The per-model admission cap for GPT-5.6 Luna in `FREEBUFF_PER_MODEL_SESSION_CAPS` is raised from 2 to 3, matching the updated `FREEBUFF_TIER_CHANGE_NOTICE` that now states Luna is 3 sessions a day. This constant is the only hard per-model ceiling tracked in the shared premium pool, so the change widens the comparison point Luna holds against the cheaper V4 Pro and Flash rows while leaving Luna on its own fixed pool. The bump is a literal edit to the caps table with no new reader or enforcement code introduced in this diff.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "audience": "maintainers",
        "evidence": "In `common/src/constants/freebuff-models.ts`, the entry `[FREEBUFF_GPT_5_6_LUNA_MODEL_ID]` within `FREEBUFF_PER_MODEL_SESSION_CAPS` changes from `limit: 2` to `limit: 3`. In `common/src/util/freebuff-model-availability.ts`, the `FREEBUFF_TIER_CHANGE_NOTICE` string literal changes from 'GPT-5.6 Luna is 2 sessions a day...' to 'GPT-5.6 Luna is 3 sessions a day...'.",
        "userVisible": false,
        "confidence": "high",
        "unknowns": "The diff does not reveal who consumes or enforces the raised Luna cap at runtime, or whether this aligns with a parallel change to Luna's cost or upstream pricing.",
