        "v": 5,
        "title": "CLI refactor: time format alias and block helper logic",
        "summary": "Refactored `formatResetTime` in `cli/src/utils/time-format.ts` to act as a typed alias for `formatResetTimeLong`, narrowing the parameter to `Date | null` while the underlying implementation accepts `Date | string | null`. Updated `cli/src/utils/message-block-helpers.ts` to replace `else if` chains with early returns and `continue` statements in `checkBlockIsUnderParent`, `extractBlockById`, and `updateToolBlockWithOutput`. The `updateToolBlockWithOutput` logic now explicitly checks for `run_terminal_command` tool names to parse stdout/stderr before falling back to generic formatting.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T04:33:22.227Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The assistant now shows a time-until-reset counter that can display days (for example, 4d 7h) and explicitly handles terminal command output before falling back to generic formatting. Developers also cleaned up how blocks of conversation are searched and updated by replacing nested if-else chains with simpler early returns and continue statements, which is behind-the-scenes housekeeping that does not change what the assistant does for the reader today.",
